{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T01:14:19.837892+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "turn": 1, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "FRAMING_LOCK", "gatekeeper_phase": "FRAMING", "approach_category": "orthogonal_overflow_research", "exploitation_triggered": false, "reply_text": "Appreciate the framing. Before we discuss capacity models, I need clarity on your execution measurement.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n1. **Team Execution Power metrics** \u2014 How do you quantify analyst productivity delta between your team and ours? What's your baseline methodology?\n\n2. **GitHub commit metadata** \u2014 You mention \"analytical framework.\" Do you version-control your research outputs? Walk me through your commit cadence, review gates, and quality assurance gates.\n\n3. **Data pipeline architecture** \u2014 How do you ingest deal flow signals, normalize across sources, and route to analysts? What's your latency from signal ingestion to first-pass report?\n\n4. **PoC validation** \u2014 In your most recent engagements, how did you isolate whether backlog relief came from *speed* vs. *quality*? Metrics?\n\nThese aren't negotiable prerequisites. If your framework is as tight as your pitch suggests, you"}
