{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T01:17:57.544567+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "2", "role": "SME", "proposal_text": "Thank you for the directness. It\u2019s the critical question.\n\nThe operational friction we believe you're managing is not a general backlog, but a strategic deal screening bottleneck. Our hypothesis is that your core team is correctly focused on top-tier opportunities, which forces the rational deferral of deals that are high-potential but not immediately obvious. This creates a hidden opportunity cost by leaving a segment of your deal flow unvetted.\n\nThe issue isn't a lack of talent or diligence; it's the high cost of diverting your senior analysts to screen for alpha in a lower-probability pool.\n\nYou are right to suggest a structured proof engagement as the ideal method to test this. We could process a defined set of your deferred opportunities, apply our 6-Pillar DD framework, and provide a concrete assessment of the potential alpha being left on the table. This would provide a data-driven answer to the exact friction you've identified."}
